e and population values for counties that currently have that K–12 teaching plans.\"}]}], \"methods_quotes\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Trends in COVID-19 incidence were analyzed using a daily 7-day moving average, aggregated by week\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"was calculated as the number of positive test results divided by the sum of positive and negative test results\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Because some data elements are incomplete for more than 47% of cases, percentages were calculated only from among those with available information.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Data represent test results, not number of persons receiving tests; test result date was used for analyses.\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"Aggregate case incidence is the rate derived after summing the case and population values for counties that currently have that K–12 teaching plans.\"}], \"confidence\": \"medium\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"study_design\"]}", "type": "text"}]}